  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1023 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nIn the long term period, we are monitoring a low pressure system\npotentially shifting from the Great Plains into the mid\nMississippi Valley on Friday into Saturday. Ahead of this, a\nfrontal boundary could push northeastward into the area and bring\nwidespread showers/thunderstorms with the assistance of an\nincreasing LLJ (~40 kts). Have continued blended guidance through\nthe weekend due to uncertainty in evolution of the system, with\nmedium to high chances of rain Saturday into Sunday. If you have\noutdoor plans this weekend, its recommended to check back in for\nthe latest forecast as we approach the end of the work week.",
